# Controls for attention-anchor.
#
# This hook is different from the guards: it prints on EVERY prompt, so "produced
# no output" cannot be its silent state. Every case therefore pins a MATCH — the
# question is never "did it speak" but "did it say the escalated part".
#
# MUTATE points the hook at a config that does not exist. It then exits early and
# says nothing at all, so every EXPECT below must go quiet.
MUTATE s|^ANCHOR_FILE=.*|ANCHOR_FILE=/nonexistent-config-15082026|

# ── sensitivity ──

EXPECT base anchor prints on an ordinary prompt
  {"prompt":"rename this variable"}
  MATCH ATTENTION ANCHOR

EXPECT escalation fires on a trigger word
  {"prompt":"please audit the sync layer"}
  MATCH full checklist

EXPECT a different trigger word also fires
  {"prompt":"prove that this is correct"}
  MATCH full checklist

# ── specificity ──

SILENT no escalation without a trigger word
  {"prompt":"rename this variable"}
  MATCH full checklist

SILENT a trigger-shaped word that is not in the list stays quiet
  {"prompt":"refactor the parser module"}
  MATCH full checklist

SILENT malformed input does not produce the escalated block
  {"not":"a prompt"}
  MATCH full checklist
